Dark Nova is a dark theme for [url=https://www.palemoon.org/]Pale Moon[/url] whose interface is inspired by the [url=https://blog.mozilla.org/en/firefox/new-firefox-design-is-here/]Mozilla Firefox Nova[/url] redesign. It is forked from [url=https://github.com/Lootyhoof/darkmoon]Dark Moon[/url], which in turn is based on [url=https://github.com/Lootyhoof/whitemoon]White Moon[/url].
[section]Features[/section]
[ul]
  [li]Nova-inspired design language: rounded surfaces, softer interaction states and more breathing room across the browser chrome.[/li]
  [li]Dark palette with a subtle cool tint and a customizable accent colour.[/li]
  [li]Fully iconized menus with [url=https://lucide.dev/]Lucide[/url] line icons: the menu bar, the context menus and their submenus.[/li]
  [li]Restyled tabs, address bar, bookmarks, menus, popups, autocomplete and find bar.[/li]
[/ul]
[section]Compatibility[/section]
Pale Moon 29.3.0 to 35.*.
[section]Credits[/section]
[ul]
  [li]Forked from Dark Moon by Lootyhoof, based on White Moon.[/li]
  [li]Icons from Lucide.[/li]
[/ul]
